---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About — WordTally"
	description="WordTally is a small, focused, client-side word, character, and readability counter. Learn what it does and why it's built this way."
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
		<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-[#221b10] sm:text-5xl">
			About WordTally
		</h1>

		<div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#4a4234]">
			<p>
				WordTally is a single-purpose writing tool: a live word, character,
				and sentence counter with reading time, speaking time, a Flesch
				readability score, and keyword density, all in one clean page.
			</p>
			<p>
				We built it deliberately small. Rather than bundling dozens of
				unrelated utilities into one bloated site, WordTally does one job
				and does it well &mdash; count and analyze your text instantly, with
				no clutter and no distractions.
			</p>
			<p>
				Everything runs entirely in your browser. There is no upload, no
				account, and no server processing your text. When you close the tab,
				nothing you typed persists anywhere.
			</p>
			<p>
				Reading time is calculated at 200 words per minute and speaking time
				at 130 words per minute &mdash; both commonly used averages for adult
				reading and presentation pacing. The readability score uses the
				Flesch Reading Ease formula with an estimated Flesch-Kincaid grade
				level, so you can see roughly how demanding your writing is to read.
				Keyword density highlights your top 10 most-used meaningful words,
				filtering out common stopwords like &ldquo;the&rdquo;,
				&ldquo;and&rdquo;, and &ldquo;is&rdquo; so you can see what your
				writing actually emphasizes.
			</p>
			<p>
				WordTally is free to use, with no signup required.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
